{
  "pages": [
    {
      "page_idx": 9,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
            0.1,
            0.104,
            0.127,
            0.119
          ],
          "content": "58"
        },
        {
          "type": "header",
          "bbox": [
            0.782,
            0.104,
            0.9,
            0.121
          ],
          "content": "MATHEMATICS"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.139,
            0.901,
            0.178
          ],
          "content": "$a _ { n }$ is also called the **general term of the AP**. If there are m terms in the AP, then $a _ { m }$ represents the **last term which is sometimes also denoted by l**."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.146,
            0.184,
            0.46,
            0.202
          ],
          "content": "Let us consider some examples."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.215,
            0.643,
            0.235
          ],
          "content": "**Example 3 :** Find the 10th term of the AP : 2, 7, 12, . . ."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.242,
            0.631,
            0.261
          ],
          "content": "**Solution :** Here, $a = 2, \\quad d = 7 - 2 = 5 \\quad  and  \\quad n = 10.$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.097,
            0.269,
            0.191,
            0.287
          ],
          "content": "We have"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.25,
            0.27,
            0.433,
            0.289
          ],
          "content": "a_{_n} = a + (n - 1) d",
          "image_source": "images/page_9_equation_7.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.097,
            0.296,
            0.135,
            0.314
          ],
          "content": "So,"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.249,
            0.295,
            0.599,
            0.316
          ],
          "content": "a_{10} = 2 + (10 - 1) \\times 5 = 2 + 45 = 47",
          "image_source": "images/page_9_equation_9.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.322,
            0.548,
            0.341
          ],
          "content": "Therefore, the 10th term of the given AP is 47."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.354,
            0.901,
            0.393
          ],
          "content": "**Example 4 :** Which term of the AP : 21, 18, 15, . . . is – 81? Also, is any term 0? Give reason for your answer."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.4,
            0.887,
            0.42
          ],
          "content": "**Solution :** Here, a = 21, d = 18 – 21 = – 3 and $a _ { _ n } = - \\; 8 1$ , and we have to find n."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.098,
            0.428,
            0.135,
            0.445
          ],
          "content": "As"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.24,
            0.428,
            0.435,
            0.448
          ],
          "content": "a_{n}=a+(n-1)d,",
          "image_source": "images/page_9_equation_14.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.097,
            0.454,
            0.187,
            0.472
          ],
          "content": "we have"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.207,
            0.453,
            0.46,
            0.525
          ],
          "content": "\\begin{aligned}- 81 &= 21 + (n - 1)(- 3) \\\\- 81 &= 24 - 3n \\\\- 105 &= - 3n \\quad  食食 \\end{aligned}",
          "image_source": "images/page_9_equation_16.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.097,
            0.534,
            0.135,
            0.552
          ],
          "content": "So,"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.244,
            0.534,
            0.322,
            0.552
          ],
          "content": "n = 3 5",
          "image_source": "images/page_9_equation_18.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.557,
            0.567,
            0.576
          ],
          "content": "Therefore, the 35th term of the given AP is – 81."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.584,
            0.899,
            0.604
          ],
          "content": "Next, we want to know if there is any n for which $a _ { _ n } = 0$ . If such an n is there, then"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.303,
            0.608,
            0.521,
            0.63
          ],
          "content": "2\\Gamma+(n-1)(-3)=0,",
          "image_source": "images/page_9_equation_21.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.098,
            0.638,
            0.139,
            0.656
          ],
          "content": "i.e.,"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.388,
            0.636,
            0.525,
            0.656
          ],
          "content": "3(n - 1) = 21",
          "image_source": "images/page_9_equation_23.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.098,
            0.664,
            0.139,
            0.682
          ],
          "content": "i.e.,"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.452,
            0.664,
            0.517,
            0.682
          ],
          "content": "n = \\; 8",
          "image_source": "images/page_9_equation_25.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.097,
            0.687,
            0.328,
            0.706
          ],
          "content": "So, the eighth term is 0."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.719,
            0.808,
            0.738
          ],
          "content": "**Example 5 :** Determine the AP whose 3rd term is 5 and the 7th term is 9."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.745,
            0.297,
            0.763
          ],
          "content": "**Solution :** We have"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.295,
            0.771,
            0.896,
            0.791
          ],
          "content": "a_{3}=a+(3-1)d=a+2d=5\\tag{1}",
          "image_source": "images/page_9_equation_29.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.097,
            0.796,
            0.142,
            0.813
          ],
          "content": "and"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.296,
            0.795,
            0.897,
            0.815
          ],
          "content": "a_{7}=a+(7-1)d=a+6d=9\\tag{2}",
          "image_source": "images/page_9_equation_31.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "bbox": [
            0.435,
            0.967,
            0.564,
            0.982
          ],
          "content": "Reprint 2026-27"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.821,
            0.616,
            0.841
          ],
          "content": "Solving the pair of linear equations (1) and (2), we get"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.397,
            0.846,
            0.541,
            0.864
          ],
          "content": "a = \\; 3 , \\quad d = 1",
          "image_source": "images/page_9_equation_34.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.097,
            0.871,
            0.503,
            0.89
          ],
          "content": "Hence, the required AP is 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, . . ."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
